Package: wsh-gst-qemu-dbus
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
Recommends: gstreamer1.0-plugins-base,
            gstreamer1.0-tools,
            qemu-server (>= 9.2.20+wsh8),
Description: GStreamer sources and input bridge for QEMU's D-Bus display
 For a streaming server on a Proxmox VE node: the GStreamer plugin qemudbus
 with two live sources, and a keyboard and mouse bridge, for a VM with the
 D-Bus display ('vga: <type>,display=dbus' or 'mesa-display=dbus' with the
 wsh-pve qemu-server, on the VM's own bus /run/wsh-dbus-display/<vmid>.sock).
 .
 qemudbussrc gives the picture of a console as raw video (BGRx for the usual
 32-bit consoles), from the pixels QEMU sends, its shared memory map of the
 console, or the dmabufs of a display with GL, which it copies out (a linear
 one mapped, a GPU's tiled one through EGL) and answers at once, so the
 guest's GL frames don't wait for the pipeline.
 qemudbusaudiosrc gives the guest's playback ('audio0: ...,driver=dbus') as
 raw PCM, scaled by the guest mixer's volume.
 .
 qemu-dbus-input reads keyboard and mouse commands from standard input (Linux
 key codes, buttons, relative and absolute motion) and sends them to the
 console, as relative or absolute motion as the guest's pointer takes it.
 .
 Run them as root or as a member of the group wsh-display.
